ARM: /proc/cpuinfo Hardware is the devicetree's model

Booted with a devicetree, every OMAP2420 board shares one machine
descriptor, so /proc/cpuinfo said "Hardware : Generic OMAP2420
(Flattened Device Tree)" on the N810. Show the devicetree's model
instead (of_flat_dt_get_machine_name(), copied, as the flat tree isn't
kept in that form): "Nokia N810". The descriptor's name stays in
dump_stack()'s hardware line.

--- a/arch/arm/kernel/setup.c
+++ b/arch/arm/kernel/setup.c
@@ -1121,6 +1121,20 @@
 
 	machine_desc = mdesc;
 	machine_name = mdesc->name;
+	/*
+	 * Booted with a devicetree, /proc/cpuinfo's Hardware line is the
+	 * board's model ("Nokia N810") rather than the shared machine
+	 * descriptor's name ("Generic OMAP2420 (Flattened Device Tree)")
+	 */
+	if (initial_boot_params) {
+		static char dt_model[64] __ro_after_init;
+		const char *model = of_flat_dt_get_machine_name();
+
+		if (model && *model) {
+			strscpy(dt_model, model, sizeof(dt_model));
+			machine_name = dt_model;
+		}
+	}
 	dump_stack_set_arch_desc("%s", mdesc->name);
 
 	if (mdesc->reboot_mode != REBOOT_HARD)
